# Privacy Policy — AI Prep MCQ

**Last updated:** April 17, 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how AI Prep MCQ ("the app", "we", "our") handles information when you use the app on your Android device. We are committed to a privacy-first approach: the app is designed to function almost entirely offline, collects no personally identifiable information, and does not share your data with third parties.

---

## 1. Information We Collect

### 1.1 Information We Do NOT Collect
We do not collect, transmit, or store:
- Your name, email address, phone number, or any contact information  
- Your location or device location data  
- Device identifiers (IMEI, advertising ID, etc.)  
- Camera, microphone, or media access  
- Contacts or calendar data  
- Usage analytics or behavioural telemetry  

The app does not require account creation or login.

### 1.2 Information Stored Locally on Your Device
All data generated by your use of the app is stored **only on your device** and is never transmitted to our servers. This includes:

- **Test history:** Your scores, answers, and completion timestamps for each test session  
- **Performance data:** Per-question accuracy tracking used to prioritise questions you find difficult  
- **XP and level progression:** Your experience points, current level, and daily XP earned  
- **Streak data:** Your daily usage streak count  
- **Preferences:** Notification settings (reminder time, daily challenge notifications), premium status, and app settings  
- **Purchase token:** Your Google Play purchase token, stored securely on your device and used solely to verify your premium purchase status  

No data from the above is ever uploaded to a server or shared with any third party.

---

## 2. Permissions Used

| Permission | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `INTERNET` | Used only to open the question reporting form (Google Forms) when you choose to report a question. The app does not use internet access for tracking, analytics, or data collection. |
| `com.android.vending.BILLING` | Required by Google Play to process the one-time premium upgrade purchase. |
| `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` | Allows the app to send optional daily study reminders and daily challenge notifications. You can disable these at any time in Settings. |
| `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED` | Used to reschedule your study reminder notifications after your device restarts. |

---

## 3. Third-Party Services

The app interacts with the following third-party services in limited, well-defined ways:

### 3.1 Google Play Billing
When you purchase the premium upgrade, the transaction is handled entirely by Google Play. We receive a purchase token to verify your purchase. We do not process payment card details. Google's privacy policy applies: https://policies.google.com/privacy

### 3.2 Google Forms (Question Reporting)
If you choose to report a question, a Google Form opens inside the app. The form may be pre-filled with the question ID and question text. Submitting the form sends that information directly to Google Forms.
Any information you choose to enter into the form is submitted by you. This feature is optional. Google's privacy policy applies: https://policies.google.com/privacy

### 3.3 No Analytics, No Advertising
The app contains **no analytics SDKs** (such as Firebase or Google Analytics), **no advertising SDKs**, and **no crash reporting services**. We do not collect or transmit any usage data.

---

## 4. Data Storage and Security

- All app data is stored locally on your device using secure storage mechanisms  
- Sensitive data such as the purchase token is stored using Android’s encrypted storage  
- The app does not back up your data to cloud services  
- If you uninstall the app, all locally stored data is permanently deleted  

---

## 5. Children's Privacy

The app does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under the age of 13. Since no personal data is collected, the app is safe for use by all age groups. If you have questions about your child's use of the app, please contact us.

